From cb7c939525fba441ff0ed32093b3b463caf96311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:01:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Telegraphs: a creature's blow drawn on the ground under it,
 its shape, reach and timing

SetTelegraph(key, unit, "wedge"|"ring", reach, arc, seconds, kind, parrySeconds, focus) lays
the blow's own shape (a wedge of its arc, or a ring all round) out to its reach, turning and
moving with the creature, and a filled copy growing from it to meet the rim as the blow lands.
A blow no guard stops is red; one that can be blocked is orange, its rim gold through the
parry's window. Not focused (meant for someone else): a faint outline. ClearTelegraph([key])
takes one away. The shapes are textures made in the client (no game file), projected through
the ground-targeting reticle's decal projector. HasActionCombat() is 7.
